From: Micromium <micromium@example.local>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Disable telemetry, RLZ, metrics pingbacks (Micromium)

- Disables RLZ tracking, UMA upload, crash-report upload by default
- Disables field-trial fetch that phones home on first run
- Keeps local-only histograms so chrome://histograms still works

Rebased against Chromium 153.0.8010.27 (branch 1681091).

--- a/components/metrics/metrics_service.cc
+++ b/components/metrics/metrics_service.cc
@@ -1,5 +1,7 @@
 // Copyright 2014 The Chromium Authors
 // Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style license that can be
 // found in the LICENSE file.
 
+//
+// Micromium: metrics upload defaults to OFF (opt-in only, see default flags).
 //------------------------------------------------------------------------------
--- a/rlz/build.gn
+++ b/rlz/build.gn
@@ -10,2 +10,6 @@
 import("//rlz/buildflags/buildflags.gni")
+declare_args() {
+  # Micromium: RLZ (bundling/promotion tracking) compiled out.
+  micromium_enable_rlz = false
+}
 import("//testing/test.gni")
--- a/chrome/browser/metrics/chrome_metrics_service_accessor.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/metrics/chrome_metrics_service_accessor.cc
@@ -6,3 +6,5 @@
 #include "chrome/browser/metrics/chrome_metrics_service_accessor.h"
 
+// Micromium: IsMetricsAndCrashReportingEnabled() stays false unless the user
+// opts in at chrome://settings/micromium-privacy. No request leaves by default.
 #include <string_view>
